@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
# Substitua os IDs pelos retornados no cadastro se o banco já tiver dados.
@payer = 1
@payee = 2

### Criar usuário comum
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ana Silva",
  "document": "11111111111",
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "senha-de-exemplo",
  "type": "COMMON"
}

### Criar lojista
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Loja Exemplo",
  "document": "22222222222222",
  "email": "loja@example.com",
  "password": "senha-de-exemplo",
  "type": "MERCHANT"
}

### Entrar como pagador
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ana@example.com", "password": "senha-de-exemplo"}

### Entrar como lojista
# @name storeLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "loja@example.com", "password": "senha-de-exemplo"}

### Consultar a própria conta
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Sem token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me

### Senha errada (401, mesma resposta de e-mail inexistente)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ana@example.com", "password": "senha-errada-123"}

### Adicionar saldo de demonstração na própria carteira (perfil demo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/{{payer}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"value": 100.00}

### Transferir (o pagador é o usuário do token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-success-001

{"value": 25.00, "payee": {{payee}}}

### Consultar saldo do pagador
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Consultar saldo do recebedor
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{storeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Consultar a carteira de outra pessoa (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{payee}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Tentar informar outro pagador no corpo (400: campo payer não é aceito)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-foreign-payer-001

{"value": 1.00, "payer": {{payee}}, "payee": {{payer}}}

### Lojista não pode pagar (422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{storeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-merchant-001

{"value": 1.00, "payee": {{payer}}}

### Saldo insuficiente (422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-insufficient-001

{"value": 1000.00, "payee": {{payee}}}

### Extrato
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/transfers?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Assistente: perguntar (exige ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; sem ela, 503)
# @name chat
POST {{baseUrl}}/assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Qual é o meu saldo e o que entrou por último?"}

### Assistente: pedir uma transferência (só cria uma proposta)
# @name proposal
POST {{baseUrl}}/assistant/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Manda R$ 10 para loja@example.com"}

### Confirmar a proposta pelo endpoint idempotente
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{proposal.response.body.proposals[0].idempotencyKey}}

{"value": {{proposal.response.body.proposals[0].value}}, "payee": {{proposal.response.body.proposals[0].payeeId}}}

### Métricas do assistente
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/wallet.assistant.tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
